cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >
  If you use GharKhata in your work, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.

type: software

title: "GharKhata"

abstract: >
  GharKhata (घर + खाता — house account ledger) is an open-source,
  over-engineered digital version of the daily expense diary found in
  every Indian household. It implements an append-only event store,
  a double-entry ledger engine with a database-enforced balance
  constraint, a config-driven category and units registry, and a
  Draft → Reviewed → Closed → Paid monthly close workflow — all behind
  a multi-tenant REST API with a schema-per-tenant PostgreSQL design.
  DHELA: Digital Household Expense Ledger App.

